		Only results whose modified is on or after this date. Date this record was created or last modified. Use this to
		restrict your data grab to changes since your last grab. (Eg, if you grab every 3 days, set modified = today
		minus 3 days.)
		"""
		minModified: String
		"""
		End of period of record for this station. Write a date as 2026-10-01, or a date and time as 2026-10-01 18:00.
		"""
		stationPorEnd: String
		"""
		Only results whose stationPorEnd is on or after this date. End of period of record for this station.
		"""
		minStationPorEnd: String
		"""
		Only results whose stationPorEnd is on or before this date. End of period of record for this station.
		"""
		maxStationPorEnd: String
		"""
		Beginning of period of record for this station. Write a date as 2026-10-01, or a date and time as 2026-10-01
		18:00.
		"""
		stationPorStart: String
		"""
		Only results whose stationPorStart is on or after this date. Beginning of period of record for this station.
		"""
		minStationPorStart: String
		"""
		Only results whose stationPorStart is on or before this date. Beginning of period of record for this station.
		"""
		maxStationPorStart: String
		"Station Type. A * at the start or the end of the value matches any text there."
		stationType: String
		"USGS Station ID. A * at the start or the end of the value matches any text there."
		usgsStationId: String
		"The DWR water district, for example 8 for the South Platte River through Denver."
		waterDistrict: Int
		"""
		Name of the water source as specified in the court case. A * at the start or the end of the value matches any
		text there.
		"""
		waterSource: String
		"""
		The WDID of a structure, the DWR identifier of seven digits, for example 0200802 for the Burlington Ditch.
		Separate several with commas.
		"""
		wdid: String
		"""
		The latitude of the centre of a location search, in decimal degrees, for example 39.7392 in Denver. Give it with
		longitude and radius.
		"""
		latitude: Float
		"""
		The longitude of the centre of a location search, in decimal degrees, for example -104.9903 in Denver.
		"""
		longitude: Float
		"""
		The radius of a location search, in the units given, up to 150 miles. Smaller values answer much faster.
		"""
		radius: Float
		"The units of the radius. Leave it out for miles."
		units: DwrRadiusUnits
		"The page to return, starting at 1. A value below 1 returns the first page."
		page: Int! = 1
		"""
		The number of results on a page, from 1 to 50. A value outside that range is moved to the nearest limit.
		"""
		size: Int! = 10
	): DwrTelemetryStationPage

