"""
A water rights call on a Colorado river: the structure that placed it, the priority it protects, and when it was
set and released.
"""
type DwrAdministrativeCall {
	"Latitude (decimal degrees) of bounding structure."
	boundingStructureLatitude: Float
	"Longitude (decimal degrees) of bounding structure."
	boundingStructureLongitude: Float
	"""
	Structure Name of upper terminus of Call; if blank, the call extends to the headwaters of the basin.
	"""
	boundingStructureName: String
	"WDID of upper terminus of Call; if blank, the call extends to the headwaters of the basin."
	boundingWdid: String
	"Unique call identifier."
	callNumber: Int
	"""
	The type of administration being described: Call, Futile Call, Nonconsumptive Call, or Authorized Diversion.
	"""
	callType: String
	"Date and time that Administrative Call all was released."
	dateTimeReleased: String
	"Date and time that Administrative Call all was set."
	dateTimeSet: String
	"DWR Water Division."
	division: Int
	"Latitude (decimal degrees) of calling structure."
	locationStructureLatitude: Float
	"Longitude (decimal degrees) of calling structure."
	locationStructureLongitude: Float
	"Call location structure name."
	locationStructureName: String
	"Call location structure WDID."
	locationWdid: String
	"Call location structure stream mile."
	locationWdidStreammile: Float
	"Last date time that this record was modified in the DWR database."
	modified: String
	"Hyperlink to additional details."
	moreInformation: String
	"""
	A calculated number developed by DWR to rank water rights in order of seniority. The priority of the water right
	is based on the appropriation date and whether the water right is subject to the Subordination Doctrine. The
	appropriation date is the date decreed by the court that the water was first put to the decreed beneficial use.
	The Subordination Doctrine established by the court says water rights that are adjudicated after other water
	rights in their stream system must be subordinate to those rights previously decreed, regardless of their
	appropriation date. To determine whether or not a water right is subject to the Subordination Doctrine, DWR
	determines the "previous adjudication date" associated with the water right.
	"""
	priorityAdminNumber: Float
	"Either the appropriation date or the previous adjudication date, whichever is earlier."
	priorityDate: String
	"An early District Court’s method to indicate a water right’s seniority in a water drainage."
	priorityNumber: String
	"""
	An order number may be assigned to distinguish decrees with identical dates but have been decreed to have
	specifically different priorities.
	"""
	priorityOrderNumber: Int
	"Waterright Structure..definition."
	priorityStructureName: String
	"Priority WDID."
	priorityWdid: String
	"Comments related to the release of the call."
	releaseComment: String
	"Comments related to setting the Administrative Call."
	setComments: String
	"Name of water source."
	waterSourceName: String
}

